# Dovecot master-user passwd-file (RFC-less, Dovecot's own format).
#
# Grants the JMAP service (worker/jmap) impersonation rights so it can open
# any mailbox's IMAP session without ever needing that mailbox's own
# password. Login as "<mailbox>*jmap_master" using this user's password
# (see auth_master_user_separator in dovecot.conf); `pass = yes` on the
# master passdb means Dovecot still verifies the destination mailbox exists
# via the normal SQL passdb, it just skips checking *its* password.
#
# The password hash below must be regenerated (via `doveadm pw -s
# SHA512-CRYPT`) if IMAP_MASTER_PASSWORD in the root .env ever changes --
# the two are independent copies of the same secret, one for Dovecot (this
# file) and one for the JMAP service (env var) to present back to Dovecot.
